# Qin et al. (2025), PASA 42, e049 (arXiv:2412.00799; the published Table A1 equals arXiv Table 3): mean Gamma_ion in 1e-12 s^-1,
#   MAP model with the [16, 84]th percentiles.
#   Posterior of a 21cmFAST-based model forward-modelling the XQR-30+ Lya forest (tau_eff distributions at z = 5.3-6.1), with
#   the UV LFs (z = 6-10) and the Planck CMB optical depth in the likelihood (fiducial model); model-based, so the z > 6 values are
#   constrained mostly through the model, not measured. Cosmology of the 21cmFAST runs not stated (values in physical units).
#   The MAP is the single best-fitting model and need not lie inside the 16-84% interval (at z = 5.64 it does not).
#   The table rounds to 0.01: where Gamma <= 0.04 (z >= 6.78) the rounding (+-0.005) is 12-50% of the value (steps in a plot).
